// fourWithHubPescDerived.recipe.jsonc — LUNAR_PRISM (P1), 2026-08-17.
//
// THE EYE GRAPH: the four certified standards with the CEDS hub, plus BOTH PESC -> CEDS derived
// bridge plugins. The sibling of fourWithHubEdfiDerived (D4) and fourWithHubSifBridge (B4), and the
// build a container named DEV_pescDerived_<YYMMDD> would be mounted from.
//
// GNC-001: it is a DEV_, and it stays one. A DEV build is never renamed to GOLD_EVAL_ without a
// round-trip PASS via `graphBuilder -goldEvalCheck --buildLogDirPath=<this build's run dir>`. That
// gate governs PROMOTION and never CREATION — any builder may make as many DEV_ scratch graphs as
// the work needs without consulting it.
//
// ⚠️ THIS RECIPE IS NOT RELEASED BY P1 OR P2 AND IS COMMITTED AHEAD OF ITS RUN DELIBERATELY, so the
// declaration is reviewable before anything is spent against it. P3 (the real-judge conformance
// batch) needs a GO WRITTEN AS DATA; P4 (the full run) IS HELD BY TQ. Judge spend is authorised PER
// LINE in acceptanceCommands.jsonc, never by the existence of a recipe.
//
// WHAT MUST NOT MOVE WHEN THIS RUNS, and it is an ASSERTION rather than an expectation: the Ed-Fi,
// SIF and CEDS base block ids. Their forges are untouched by this order. A moved Ed-Fi, SIF or CEDS
// id is a DEFECT, not a re-key, and the run stops. The PESC base block and the four-forge manifest
// DID move, once, as the named mover of RULING P1-R8. BOTH ENDPOINTS ARE STATED WITH THEIR BUILD MODE
// (RULING P2-R4) because a block refId is a content address over block TEXT and the text CONTAINS the
// embeddings — so an id is only comparable to another computed under the SAME vectorisation flag:
//   pesc260805 base   045523dc197f4649712b74d3d6b995522106d44fa5c17c17d900205c4ee4a992  [vectorize=true]
//                  -> f139654a98cd0ef238759e6dc2bda2e532f13d5a7db00bfea94d89c3317b149d  [vectorize=true]
//   four-forge manifest 7e8372a2f342dffd5999e2e50e00bf69aa83f698ea980849f96ab568e42ab00a
//                    -> 09cb194a7313e184fbff9bc3f6a5e21265c9dcea8bb2f8068ad0ec6b1664d24b
//
// ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-17, AND THE SUPERSEDED VALUES ARE NAMED HERE RATHER THAN ERASED. This header
// previously read `-> c46991d1…` and `-> 96815028…`. Those were computed from a `--vectorize=false`
// re-forge — a VECTORLESS artifact, not a member of this lineage. The flag had been chosen deliberately
// to make embedding spend zero BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by cache hit, which was the stronger safety
// guarantee; THE SAFETY MEASURE CHANGED THE IDENTITY OF THE THING IT WAS PROTECTING. Nothing in the
// record could have revealed it, because the lineage carried no field naming the build mode — which is
// precisely the field RULING P2-R4 now requires. See forges/pesc260805/bridgeData/buildModeIdentityRecord.json.
//
// Both current values computed by REFERENCE COMPOSITION (test/probes/p2_composeManifestCorrected.js),
// which reproduces THREE historical manifest ids — including the superseded one, which is what proves
// the tool was never at fault, only its input — and needs no build at all. Its predecessor
// p1_composeManifestFromReferences.js is left UNEDITED as the retained evidence behind the wrong figure.
//
// THE TWO POPULATIONS' STATISTICS ARE REPORTED SEPARATELY AND NEVER POOLED — see the eval sibling's
// header for why. That rule survives into every artifact this recipe produces.
{
	"schemaVersion": "1.0.0",
	"recipeName": "fourWithHubPescDerived",
	"kind": "dev",
	"description": "The four certified standards with the CEDS hub, PLUS both PESC -> CEDS DERIVED bridge plugins (pescCedsDerivedPlugin over PescElementDecl, pescOptionSetCedsDerivedPlugin over PescNamedDefinition) — the eye graph for P4.",
	"standards": [
		{ "token": "ceds", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "edfi", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "pesc260805", "version": "current" },
		{ "token": "sif", "version": "current" }
	],
	"hubs": [
		{ "standard": "ceds" }
	],
	// ⚠️ THE PROPERTY TIER ONLY, AND THE OPTION-SET TIER'S ABSENCE IS DECLARED RATHER THAN SILENT.
	// RULING P2-R5. This recipe previously declared BOTH PESC plugins and could not be built: two derived
	// plugins over one standard pair compose an IDENTICAL manifest subject, and a four-forge graph is ONE
	// MANIFEST by definition, so a single four-standard graph CANNOT contain both PESC tiers. See
	// pescDerivedEval.recipe.jsonc's header for the composer code facts.
	//
	// WHY THE PROPERTY TIER IS THE ONE NAMED HERE: it is the tier the entire P0/P0b measurement chain
	// describes. That is a reason, not a ranking.
	//
	// THE OPTION-SET TIER'S EYE GRAPH IS A SEPARATE GRAPH PENDING A DELIVERABLE RULING — it is NOT
	// dropped, NOT deferred for convenience, and NOT out of scope. The supervisor is ruling it separately
	// and informing TQ, because it changes what he RECEIVES rather than how it is built. AN OMISSION THAT
	// IS NOT DECLARED IS INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM AN OVERSIGHT, which is the only reason this paragraph
	// exists. The option-set bridge itself is shipped, validated, and censused (223/223 judged, zero
	// orphans, zero collisions, block c8dbb1f9) — nothing about it is unfinished.
	"bridges": [
		{ "source": "pesc260805", "hub": "ceds", "bridge": "pescCedsDerivedPlugin", "dependencies": ["pesc260805", "ceds"] }
	],
	"roundTripStage": true
}
